title Portage r1 — value carried across two worlds, atomic on both ledgers or neither
prompt take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the 1024-round / double-seat road; approve own design rounds; double-seat visions for blind spots; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates
think Read REMEMBER + the 1024-round itinerary + the six-season double-seat expansion. The loop had just closed the Freight world-state-migration arc (r1-r4) end to end and folded it onto REMEMBER. All four Freight witnesses re-run GREEN — the arc stands.
think Lindy-first crux-first across the whole road: Season D built how nodes AGREE within one order (Cord..Warrant), placed which host runs which world (Puddle), and moved a world's whole state across a re-berth (Freight). Every coin so far lived and died inside ONE Cord. The highest-value still-tractable blind spot is the one no single-world ledger can answer and the vision names explicitly (beat TigerBeetle/Mysticeti): value crossing BETWEEN two worlds, atomic on both ledgers or neither — cross-shard settlement.
think The content-addressed grain makes the crossing free and safe, mirroring Freight's insight: bind the two halves of the transfer by a SHA-256 digest over id.amount.from.to_world.to_account, so a receiving world credits ONLY a digest it can verify against the sending world's burn. The decision is a pure function of both ledgers' bytes — no correspondent to trust.
think Named the journey Portage per the comlink-tendency + the Puddle/Freight water family — goods carried between two navigable waters that share no channel, exactly a transfer between two ledgers with no shared order. Grep-confirmed collision-free tree-wide.
think Wrote portage as its OWN two-world fold law (mirroring how Pledge wrote its own over the shared signed facts), rather than bending lapse/statement which know only P/H/V tags. resolve_world(dag, verify) folds kind_issue (credit), tag_out (debit the signer, record the world's burn digest), tag_in (credit the recipient ONLY when its embedded digest equals the verified burn's, else NoMatchingBurn).
obs r1 built GREEN. One build fix on metal: scene 3 minted two byte-identical in-blocks (same gateway/id/digest) so cord.add refused Duplicate; a DISTINCT gateway re-presenting the same crossing id yields distinct blocks, one crossing — the AlreadyLanded refusal it was meant to prove.
obs Four scenes: the crux (Alice on A debited by exactly amount, Bob on B credited by exactly amount, the pair conserves left==reached==40, the two worlds' order-heads distinct so it is a real crossing); NoMatchingBurn (an in whose digest matches no verified burn refuses, and a receiving world with no verified burn at all refuses just the same); AlreadyLanded (a second in for one id refuses — the crossing lands once); NeverPaid (a burn beyond the signer's balance refuses — a debit cannot be conjured either).
obs Composed cord + fold + voucher + kumara public API only, editing none — the Voucher order-head and the Pledge two-phase transfer both re-run GREEN at the witness door. TAME bans clean (portage.rye carries many asserts, not on the zero-assert ratchet; no usize, no std.debug.assert, no memcpy, no compound assert); width-check exits clean.
obs Custody untouched — demo world/keeper seeds only, no key/funds/network, no value crossed. A served portage (World B fetching World A's out-fact over Comlink) reaches the Comlink-served gate; a real Aurora host for either world reaches gates #2/#4. No gate reached this round.
